                "text": "Method B uses a lipophilic (oil-based) emulsifier applied undiluted by immersion, acting fast on contact. Method D uses a hydrophilic (water-dilutable, detergent-type) emulsifier with a pre-rinse and controlled concentration, giving finer removal control. Method D dominates modern aerospace FPI lines precisely because its variables are measurable and enforceable."
