                "text": "Eight weeks is a realistic floor if the firm already performs the work competently and the gap is documentary. The long poles are the written practice signature, procedure rewrites with traceable essential variables, and personnel files that have to be reconstructed rather than corrected. Firms starting with no Appendix B programme at all should plan on a longer runway, because commercial grade dedication and 10 CFR 21 procedures have to be written from scratch."
